- #2162 (voter zram), awaiting blahaj review;
- #2161 (hashed lock), awaiting a sting lockfile run;
- waifu-mirror#15, awaiting the blahaj digest check and apply.

## 2026-10-04 ~01:50Z: lab seat (neo), R-C241: sting seat-isolation split and drivers (operator interview; blahaj carrier TIN-5128 880c5e74)

**The split.** The operator ruled the split as proposed. Each repo writes only the unit scope it already writes, and contract tests on both sides refuse writes to the other repo's paths.

**Blahaj node_hygiene drives these.** Each lands as a source PR first, then an attended converge:
- sshd MemoryMin 256M and CPUWeight 1000;
- kubelet system-reserved memory 3Gi;
- user-1000.slice re-armed at MemoryHigh 26G / MemoryMax 30G, superseding 20889M/24G;
- systemd-oomd enabled with the root policy, and avoid set on sshd.service.

Blahaj is also writing the design spec (`docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-04-voter-dev-seat-isolation-design.md`) and studying CRS QoS (xoxd-ai/crs310-8g-2s-in): DSCP for ssh and the cmux relay, queue trees, and tailnet direct vs DERP.

**Lab drives these** through Home Manager user units:
- a `tinyland-heavy` user slice nested inside the 26G high, leaving headroom for CLion, junie and interactive sessions;
- a `systemd-run --user` wrapper for agent heavy jobs (ML, TLC, bazel, cargo, GHC). It is opt-in and caps nothing outside itself (no containment);
- per-unit ManagedOOMPreference: avoid for tmux, cmux and ssh helpers, prefer for heavy scopes;
- a contract test in which lab refuses to write sshd, user-1000.slice, kubelet or the oomd root config.

**R32 cgroup v2 delegation (TIN-2730)** is co-designed by blahaj and GF. Lab writes only what the host side needs, through blahaj #1467.

Operator, verbatim: "blahaj already proposed each of these, consider / establish who is driving these (collaborate)".

**2026-09-25: R-N11 edge cases (R-N13 receipt)**

The operator answered **"Leave all as they are"**. No further change to #1913 for these:
- double force (`--force --force`) keeps passing like the plain form;
- idle-sleep timers (`pmset -a sleep N`, `systemsetup -setcomputersleep`) keep passing;
- masking sleep targets stays refused under the aggregate-unit rule.

The note keeps them listed as known edges.

**Ruling 2026-09-23, R-N90: W4 io layer starts now, in parallel with W3.**

Scope:
- the sys_darwin/sys_linux syscall wrappers, with an io-trace feature;
- the R-N88 crash-state checker;
- the buf.rs aligned slab pool;
- the fused FastCDC+BLAKE3 chunker, backed by a bit-identical proptest.

It is standalone and unit-proven, and it is not wired into the v3 path. W3 owns durable.rs; W4 integration will reconcile durable.rs onto the sys_* layer. Tracked in bulkload#46.

**Probe 1 recorded — 2026-08-24T05:53:50Z** (script-produced artifact, first run of the new `just sting-adoption-evidence` probe; PR [lab#1429](https://github.com/tinyland-inc/lab/pull/1429), auto-merge armed):

```json
{
  "schema": "dev.tinyland.sting-adoption-evidence.v1",
  "criteria": {
    "who_nonempty": false,
    "tmux_main_alive": true,
    "sting_side_pr": true,
    "sting_side_pr_note": "static true via lab#1402 (merged); not re-derived"
  },
  "probes": {
    "tmux_ls": "main: 1 windows (created Sat Aug 22 09:02:33 2026)",
    "loginctl": "6 sessions incl. jess manager (1) + user sessions c1372/c282/c604"
  },
  "signals_sent": 0, "writes_on_target": 0
}
```

**Reading:** criteria 2 and 3 are MET (tmux `main` continuously alive since 08-22 09:02 EDT — through the honey incident, the GF window gating, and three neo crashes; criterion 3 via merged #1402). Criterion 1 (`who` non-empty) reads false **by probe construction**: `who` reports controlling-tty logins only, and a BatchMode `ssh -n` probe never appears in it — loginctl simultaneously shows six live sessions including three jess user sessions. An interactive landing session (the boundary's STING_FIRST_HOUR walk) satisfies it naturally. No criterion-definition change requested; probe 2 (≥24h later, i.e. after 2026-08-25T05:53Z) runs post-landing and should show 3/3. Deadline margin: 3+ days to 08-27T12:12Z.

**Second queue entry observed — no second mutation**

At `2026-08-17T08:04:44Z`, after the protective dequeue above, GitHub recorded a new user-origin enqueue by `Jesssullivan`:
- entry `MQE_lQDORVPWj87_x01gzgADh3DOAo1N1g`, position 1, `AWAITING_CHECKS`;
- merge-group head `bbd6828257567968be126e3b2bf3804344221786`, tree `d64db29805d18d4bb97929d453b8fe9a3b74a2a3`, ordered parents `[f08c4a9a…, 7e3888b0…]`;
- fresh Tracker run `32008673113` and legacy Validate run `32008673009`.

Protected main and PR source head remain unchanged. This lane will not fight a repeated user-origin transition: no second dequeue/cancel/edit was performed. The prior zero-hosted, Fish/cockpit P1, and no-activation findings remain in force. Explicit operator direction is required to reconcile the repeated enqueue with those gates.

